{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794452506","published":"2026-11-12T03:02:00Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:34.235183031Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-107364","CVE-2026-112314","CVE-2026-112320","CVE-2026-112321","CVE-2026-112322","CVE-2026-112323","CVE-2026-118380","CVE-2026-119079","CVE-2026-71199","CVE-2026-71200"],"summary":"Fix of 10 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: multiple vulnerabilities fixed in MIT krb5 1.22.3\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-71199.patch: reject unkeyed checksums in\n       CAMMAC verifiers\n     - CVE-2026-71199\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-71200.patch: prevent a null dereference in\n       PKINIT CMS processing\n     - CVE-2026-71200\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-112320.patch: release the RPCSEC_GSS context\n       when a client switches auth flavor\n     - CVE-2026-112320\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-112314.patch: free the RPC reply verifier\n       between clnttcp_call() retries\n     - CVE-2026-112314\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-112321.patch: free AUTH_GSSAPI call\n       arguments on all exit paths\n     - CVE-2026-112321\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-107364.patch: prevent a KDC read overrun in\n       fetch_asn1_field()\n     - CVE-2026-107364\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-112322-CVE-2026-112323.patch: disable the\n       AUTH_GSSAPI RPC flavor unless GSSRPC_ALLOW_AUTH_GSSAPI is set\n     - CVE-2026-112322\n     - CVE-2026-112323\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-118380.patch: use the verified RPCSEC_GSS\n       service level for each call\n     - CVE-2026-118380\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119079.patch: avoid quadratic reallocation\n       when decoding ASN.1 sequences\n     - CVE-2026-119079","affected":[{"package":{"name":"krb5-admin-server","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/krb5-admin-server?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.17-3+deb10u6+tuxcare.els2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-os